n. How does the parser handle multiple arguments? Let me look at how call args are parsed. There might be record-literal arguments or tuple-like. Let me look at the parser.\n\nLet me check how `range(1000)` and other calls are parsed, and whether multi-argument calls exist. jq's `sort_by(.key)` is a two-arg call. In toylang, functions are unary (per \"Functions the language provides. Unary like every other function\"). So how would `sort_by(.key)` be spelled? Maybe as `sort_by(v, .key)`? Let me look at the parser to see if multi-arg calls are supported.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_068ca46f3001LOJhkvb0ufDW2R","sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","messageID":"msg_068ca3b440015biFjzfV8J6720"}}
