{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788464494789,"sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_107f0f31a8644b9996636624","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls tests/corpus | grep -iE 'sort|max'"},"output":"max_empty_unwrap_refuses.yaml\nmax_empty.yaml\nmax_int64s.yaml\nmax_ints.yaml\nmax_negative.yaml\nsort_chars.yaml\nsort_descending.yaml\nsort_int64s.yaml\nsort_ints.yaml\nsort_strs.yaml\n","metadata":{"output":"max_empty_unwrap_refuses.yaml\nmax_empty.yaml\nmax_int64s.yaml\nmax_ints.yaml\nmax_negative.yaml\nsort_chars.yaml\nsort_descending.yaml\nsort_int64s.yaml\nsort_ints.yaml\nsort_strs.yaml\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls tests/corpus | grep -iE 'sort|max'","time":{"start":1788464494784,"end":1788464494787}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting — the issue says this example \"replaces its hand-written best_of comparator\". Wait, the plan says `best_of` and `find_best` are the max implementations. Hmm, the issue says `docs/examples/euler/26-reciprocal-cycles.md` (replaces its hand-written best_of comparator). Hmm but in this file, `find_best` is a halving search — it's not a straight max over a Vec. Actually the max_by would be `max_by(cycle_length)` applied to a Vec of `{d, len}` records... Wait, the plan says problem 26 needs to compute max over `{d, len}` pairs compared by `.len`. But the file's `find_best` uses a halving recursion (for stack depth reasons). With `max` builtin, you could do `range(999) | map({d: . + 2, len: cycle_length(. + 2)}) | max_by(.len)`.\n\n Let me not overthink the example rewriting yet — the primary task is implementing sort_by and max_by across backends. The examples updates might be part of it (unblocks docs/examples/euler/26 and 22). But the brief says \"Implement across all backends, following the existing sort/max builtins as reference. Unblocks docs/examples/euler/26... and docs/examples/euler/22...\" So I likely need to update those example docs too. But maybe just the implementation is the priority; the examples update could be a follow-up. Let me focus first on the implementation, then handle the docs/examples.\n\nLet me look at the tests/docs.rs that insists each builtin has a reference page, and how the reference pages are tested. Also check corpus tests for sort/max to understand the testing pattern.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_068ca789d001YUlt3OI78wZIyy","sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","messageID":"msg_068ca6a5f001wv4PDpD6HPxVAO"}}
