eady read, generalised to rebuild the object instead.\n        Kind::OptMap {\n            source,\n            param,\n            body,\n        } => format!(\n            \"({} | if . == \\\"none\\\" then \\\"none\\\" else (.some as {} | {{some: {}}}) end)\",\n            expr(enums, source),\n            local(*param),","lineStart":555,"lineEnd":664,"totalLines":940,"truncated":true}},"title":"src/emit_jq.rs","time":{"start":1788464559948,"end":1788464559961}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have a good understanding of the Rust backend. Let me look at the other backends' handling of Sort/Max and Map in expr context. Let me read:\n- emit_jq.rs around 560-640 (Sort/Max, Map)\n- emit_js.rs around 840-950\n- emit_lua.rs around 860-940\n- emit_go.rs around 1060-1180\n- emit_llvm.rs around 1420-1460 and the runtime functions\n- emit_toylang.rs (round-trip emitter","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_068cb7344001qHmZvrDQdrcrvk","sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","messageID":"msg_068cb68aa0015F2br0J6iKR1iu"}}
