{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788464605814,"sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_50f207751c2d4e768c165984","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/tests/corpus/map_guard_chain_over_vec_field.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/tests/corpus/map_guard_chain_over_vec_field.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # A guard chain over `.` inside map: the native backend used to evaluate the match's subject\n2: # eagerly even for a pure guard chain, which never reads the subject as a whole value. That\n3: # forced a whole-record read out of the struct-of-arrays cursor `map` binds `.` to, which native\n4: # cannot do (issue #40). `.readings[0]` is the field-then-index shape that surfaced it.\n5: program: |\n6:   [{valid: 1 == 2, readings: [5]}, {valid: 1 == 1, readings: [1]}]\n7:       | map(.valid -> .readings[0]! or any() -> 0)\n8: \n9: output: |\n10:   [0,1]\n11: \n12: node_types: [compare.eq, int, local, map-over, match, pipe, projection, record-literal, selection.collapse, unwrap, vec-literal]\n\n(End of file - total 12 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# A guard chain over `.` inside map: the native backend used to evaluate the match's subject\n# eagerly even for a pure guard chain, which never reads the subject as a whole value. That\n# forced a whole-record read out of the struct-of-arrays cursor `map` binds `.` to, which native\n# cannot do (issue #40). `.readings[0]` is the field-then-index shape that surfaced it.\nprogram: |\n  [{valid: 1 == 2, readings: [5]}, {valid: 1 == 1, readings: [1]}]\n      | map(.valid -> .readings[0]! or any() -> 0)\n\noutput: |\n  [0,1]\n\nnode_types: [compare.eq, int, local, map-over, match, pipe, projection, record-literal, selection.collapse, unwrap, vec-literal]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/tests/corpus/map_guard_chain_over_vec_field.yaml","text":"# A guard chain over `.` inside map: the native backend used to evaluate the match's subject\n# eagerly even for a pure guard chain, which never reads the subject as a whole value. That\n# forced a whole-record read out of the struct-of-arrays cursor `map` binds `.` to, which native\n# cannot do (issue #40). `.readings[0]` is the field-then-index shape that surfaced it.\nprogram: |\n  [{valid: 1 == 2, readings: [5]}, {valid: 1 == 1, readings: [1]}]\n      | map(.valid -> .readings[0]! or any() -> 0)\n\noutput: |\n  [0,1]\n\nnode_types: [compare.eq, int, local, map-over, match, pipe, projection, record-literal, selection.collapse, unwrap, vec-literal]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":12,"totalLines":12,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/map_guard_chain_over_vec_field.yaml","time":{"start":1788464605809,"end":1788464605813}},"id":"prt_068cc2a6f001UhPAuv64LYtD4m","sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","messageID":"msg_068cc23e10013mcrVGV47fGz8X"}}
