{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788464664565,"sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1416ef4d02724c328c9d2779","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/emit_llvm.rs","limit":130,"offset":1260},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/emit_llvm.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1260:                 // The struct-of-arrays boundary. Nothing in the language asks for a whole\n1261:                 // element out of a Vec, so this is unreachable until an indexing operator\n1262:                 // exists; printing gathers through the runtime instead.\n1263:                 Some(Slot::Cursor { .. }) => {\n1264:                     return Err(unsupported(\"using a Vec element as a whole value\"));\n1265:                 }\n1266:                 None => return Err(format!(\"local {id} is not bound in the native backend\")),\n1267:             },\n1268: \n1269:             Kind::Bind { local, value, body } => {\n1270:                 let value = self.expr(value)?;\n1271:                 self.locals.insert(*local, Slot::Value(value));\n1272:                 self.expr(body)?\n1273:             }\n1274: \n1275:             Kind::Call { func, arg } => {\n1276:                 let args = self.call_args(arg)?;\n1277:                 let callee = *self\n1278:                     .funcs\n1279:                     .get(func)\n1280:                     .ok_or_else(|| format!(\"`{func}` was never declared\"))?;\n1281:                 self.builder\n1282:                     .build_call(callee, &args, \"call\")\n1283:                     .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n1284:                     .try_as_basic_value()\n1285:                     .basic()\n1286:                     .ok_or_else(|| \"a toylang function returned nothing\".to_string())?\n1287:             }\n1288: \n1289:             Kind::Concat(l, r) => self.concat(&t.ty, l, r)?,\n1290: \n1291:             Kind::Compare { op, lhs, rhs } => self.compare(*op, lhs, rhs)?,\n1292: \n1293:             Kind::Logic { op, lhs, rhs } => self.logic(*op, lhs, rhs)?,\n1294: \n1295:             // A Bool is an i1 here, so a bitwise complement is the whole of it.\n1296:             Kind::Not(base) => {\n1297:                 let v = self.expr(base)?.into_int_value();\n1298:                 self.builder\n1299:                     .build_not(v, \"not\")\n1300:                     .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n1301:                     .into()\n1302:             }\n1303: \n1304:             // Fields are in declaration order, so field `i` here is field `i` of the type,\n1305:             // which is what every reader of the record relies on.\n1306:             Kind::RecordLit { fields } => {\n1307:                 let i64t = self.ctx.i64_type();\n1308:                 let rec = self\n1309:                     .call_rt(\n1310:                         self.rt.rec_new,\n1311:                         &[i64t.const_int(fields.len() as u64, false).into()],\n1312:                         \"rec\",\n1313:                     )?\n1314:                     .into_pointer_value();\n1315:                 for (i, (_, value)) in fields.iter().enumerate() {\n1316:                     let built = self.expr(value)?;\n1317:                     let slot = self.to_slot(built, &value.ty)?;\n1318:                     self.builder\n1319:                         .build_call(\n1320:                             self.rt.rec_set,\n1321:                             &[\n1322:                                 rec.into(),\n1323:                                 i64t.const_int(i as u64, false).into(),\n1324:                                 slot.into(),\n1325:                             ],\n1326:                             \"\",\n1327:                         )\n1328:                         .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n1329:                 }\n1330:                 rec.into()\n1331:             }\n1332: \n1333:             Kind::EnumLit { variant, payload } => {\n1334:                 if t.ty.as_opt().is_some() {\n1335:                     return self.opt_lit(payload.as_deref());\n1336:                 }\n1337:                 self.enum_lit(&t.ty, variant, payload.as_deref())?\n1338:             }\n1339: \n1340:             Kind::VecLit(items) => {\n1341:                 let elem =\n1342:                     t.ty.elem()\n1343:                         .ok_or_else(|| \"a Vec literal that is not a Vec\".to_string())?\n1344:                         .clone();\n1345:                 self.vec_lit(items, &elem)?\n1346:             }\n1347: \n1348:             Kind::Select {\n1349:                 source,\n1350:                 param,\n1351:                 pred,\n1352:             } => self.select(source, *param, pred)?,\n1353: \n1354:             Kind::Map {\n1355:                 source,\n1356:                 param,\n1357:                 body,\n1358:             } => self.map(source, *param, body, &t.ty)?,\n1359: \n1360:             // The stream, materialized eagerly: whatever consumes it -- `collect`, a mapper --\n1361:             // works on the Vec of its entries.\n1362:             Kind::Lines => self.call_rt(self.rt.collect_lines, &[], \"lines\")?,\n1363: \n1364:             // Same raw lines as `lines`, each split on the delimiter into one row. The delimiter\n1365:             // rides as a string constant, so the split is literal on every backend.\n1366:             Kind::Dsv { delim } => {\n1367:                 let lines = self.call_rt(self.rt.collect_lines, &[], \"lines\")?;\n1368:                 let sep = self.string_const(delim);\n1369:                 self.call_rt(self.rt.split_lines, &[lines, sep.into()], \"rows\")?\n1370:             }\n1371: \n1372:             Kind::Input => {\n1373:                 let global = self\n1374:                     .input_slot\n1375:                     .ok_or_else(|| \"an `input` node the module never read stdin for\".to_string())?;\n1376:                 let slot = self\n1377:                     .builder\n1378:                     .build_load(self.ctx.i64_type(), global, \"input_slot\")\n1379:                     .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n1380:                     .into_int_value();\n1381:                 self.read_slot(slot, &t.ty)?\n1382:             }\n1383: \n1384:             // Already a proper Vec pointer, unlike Input's raw slot: tl_read_inputs assembles\n1385:             // it itself, so there is nothing here for read_slot to unpack.\n1386:             Kind::Inputs => {\n1387:                 let elem =\n1388:                     crate::tir::runtime_elem(&t.ty).expect(\"checked to be Vec<T> or Stream<T>\");\n1389:                 let descriptor = self.string_const(&descriptor(self.enums, elem));\n\n(Showing lines 1260-1389 of 2664. Use offset=1390 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"                // The struct-of-arrays boundary. Nothing in the language asks for a whole\n                // element out of a Vec, so this is unreachable until an indexing operator\n                // exists; printing gathers through the runtime instead.\n                Some(Slot::Cursor { .. }) => {\n                    return Err(unsupported(\"using a Vec element as a whole value\"));\n                }\n                None => return Err(format!(\"local {id} is not bound in the native backend\")),\n            },\n\n            Kind::Bind { local, value, body } => {\n                let value = self.expr(value)?;\n                self.locals.insert(*local, Slot::Value(value));\n                self.expr(body)?\n            }\n\n            Kind::Call { func, arg } => {\n                let args = self.call_args(arg)?;\n                let callee = *self\n                    .funcs\n                    .get(func)","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/emit_llvm.rs","text":"                // The struct-of-arrays boundary. Nothing in the language asks for a whole\n                // element out of a Vec, so this is unreachable until an indexing operator\n                // exists; printing gathers through the runtime instead.\n                Some(Slot::Cursor { .. }) => {\n                    return Err(unsupported(\"using a Vec element as a whole value\"));\n                }\n                None => return Err(format!(\"local {id} is not bound in the native backend\")),\n            },\n\n            Kind::Bind { local, value, body } => {\n                let value = self.expr(value)?;\n                self.locals.insert(*local, Slot::Value(value));\n                self.expr(body)?\n            }\n\n            Kind::Call { func, arg } => {\n                let args = self.call_args(arg)?;\n                let callee = *self\n                    .funcs\n                    .get(func)\n                    .ok_or_else(|| format!(\"`{func}` was never declared\"))?;\n                self.builder\n                    .build_call(callee, &args, \"call\")\n                    .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n                    .try_as_basic_value()\n                    .basic()\n                    .ok_or_else(|| \"a toylang function returned nothing\".to_string())?\n            }\n\n            Kind::Concat(l, r) => self.concat(&t.ty, l, r)?,\n\n            Kind::Compare { op, lhs, rhs } => self.compare(*op, lhs, rhs)?,\n\n            Kind::Logic { op, lhs, rhs } => self.logic(*op, lhs, rhs)?,\n\n            // A Bool is an i1 here, so a bitwise complement is the whole of it.\n            Kind::Not(base) => {\n                let v = self.expr(base)?.into_int_value();\n                self.builder\n                    .build_not(v, \"not\")\n                    .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n                    .into()\n            }\n\n            // Fields are in declaration order, so field `i` here is field `i` of the type,\n            // which is what every reader of the record relies on.\n            Kind::RecordLit { fields } => {\n                let i64t = self.ctx.i64_type();\n                let rec = self\n                    .call_rt(\n                        self.rt.rec_new,\n                        &[i64t.const_int(fields.len() as u64, false).into()],\n                        \"rec\",\n                    )?\n                    .into_pointer_value();\n                for (i, (_, value)) in fields.iter().enumerate() {\n                    let built = self.expr(value)?;\n                    let slot = self.to_slot(built, &value.ty)?;\n                    self.builder\n                        .build_call(\n                            self.rt.rec_set,\n                            &[\n                                rec.into(),\n                                i64t.const_int(i as u64, false).into(),\n                                slot.into(),\n                            ],\n                            \"\",\n                        )\n                        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n                }\n                rec.into()\n            }\n\n            Kind::EnumLit { variant, payload } => {\n                if t.ty.as_opt().is_some() {\n                    return self.opt_lit(payload.as_deref());\n                }\n                self.enum_lit(&t.ty, variant, payload.as_deref())?\n            }\n\n            Kind::VecLit(items) => {\n                let elem =\n                    t.ty.elem()\n                        .ok_or_else(|| \"a Vec literal that is not a Vec\".to_string())?\n                        .clone();\n                self.vec_lit(items, &elem)?\n            }\n\n            Kind::Select {\n                source,\n                param,\n                pred,\n            } => self.select(source, *param, pred)?,\n\n            Kind::Map {\n                source,\n                param,\n                body,\n            } => self.map(source, *param, body, &t.ty)?,\n\n            // The stream, materialized eagerly: whatever consumes it -- `collect`, a mapper --\n            // works on the Vec of its entries.\n            Kind::Lines => self.call_rt(self.rt.collect_lines, &[], \"lines\")?,\n\n            // Same raw lines as `lines`, each split on the delimiter into one row. The delimiter\n            // rides as a string constant, so the split is literal on every backend.\n            Kind::Dsv { delim } => {\n                let lines = self.call_rt(self.rt.collect_lines, &[], \"lines\")?;\n                let sep = self.string_const(delim);\n                self.call_rt(self.rt.split_lines, &[lines, sep.into()], \"rows\")?\n            }\n\n            Kind::Input => {\n                let global = self\n                    .input_slot\n                    .ok_or_else(|| \"an `input` node the module never read stdin for\".to_string())?;\n                let slot = self\n                    .builder\n                    .build_load(self.ctx.i64_type(), global, \"input_slot\")\n                    .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n                    .into_int_value();\n                self.read_slot(slot, &t.ty)?\n            }\n\n            // Already a proper Vec pointer, unlike Input's raw slot: tl_read_inputs assembles\n            // it itself, so there is nothing here for read_slot to unpack.\n            Kind::Inputs => {\n                let elem =\n                    crate::tir::runtime_elem(&t.ty).expect(\"checked to be Vec<T> or Stream<T>\");\n                let descriptor = self.string_const(&descriptor(self.enums, elem));","lineStart":1260,"lineEnd":1389,"totalLines":2664,"truncated":true}},"title":"src/emit_llvm.rs","time":{"start":1788464664548,"end":1788464664563}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The LLVM backend is the most complex. Let me now understand how the LLVM emitter handles Map/Select, to figure out how to emit SortBy/MaxBy. The projection body in LLVM runs per element — but in LLVM, the Map node's body is emitted as an expression with the param bound to... a Slot. Let me look at the LLVM Map/Select emission around line 1348.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_068cd0fda001N1M1S0jXBPGefK","sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","messageID":"msg_068ccff91001TDPve5koYEl83W"}}
