{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788464724271,"sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4ada049ec51741c1b49d6330","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs","limit":90,"offset":519},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n519: \n520: /// Every node in the tree, `t` itself included, in no particular order. The backends each walk\n521: /// the tree their own way, gathering what their own target needs; this is for the questions\n522: /// that are the same on every target. Public so `offload::explain` can report on every\n523: /// sub-expression the same way. \n524: pub fn each_node(t: &Tir, f: &mut impl FnMut(&Tir)) {\n525:     f(t);\n526:     match &t.kind {\n527:         Kind::Str(_)\n528:         | Kind::Int(_)\n529:         | Kind::Float(_)\n530:         | Kind::Var(_)\n531:         | Kind::Local(_)\n532:         | Kind::Input\n533:         | Kind::Inputs\n534:         | Kind::Lines\n535:         | Kind::Dsv { .. } => {}\n536:         Kind::VecLit(items) => items.iter().for_each(|i| each_node(i, f)),\n537:         Kind::RecordLit { fields } => fields.iter().for_each(|(_, v)| each_node(v, f)),\n538:         Kind::EnumLit { payload, .. } => {\n539:             if let Some(p) = payload {\n540:                 each_node(p, f);\n541:             }\n542:         }\n543:         Kind::Call { arg, .. } => {\n544:             if let Some(a) = arg {\n545:                 each_node(a, f);\n546:             }\n547:         }\n548:         Kind::Concat(l, r)\n549:         | Kind::Compare { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. }\n550:         | Kind::Logic { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. }\n551:         | Kind::Arith { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. } => {\n552:             each_node(l, f);\n553:             each_node(r, f);\n554:         }\n555:         Kind::Not(base) => each_node(base, f),\n556:         Kind::Bind { value, body, .. } => {\n557:             each_node(value, f);\n558:             each_node(body, f);\n559:         }\n560:         Kind::Map { source, body, .. } | Kind::OptMap { source, body, .. } => {\n561:             each_node(source, f);\n562:             each_node(body, f);\n563:         }\n564:         Kind::Select { source, pred, .. } => {\n565:             each_node(source, f);\n566:             each_node(pred, f);\n567:         }\n568:         Kind::Field { base, .. } | Kind::Unwrap { base } => each_node(base, f),\n569:         Kind::Builtin { arg, .. } => each_node(arg, f),\n570:         Kind::Index { base, index, .. } => {\n571:             each_node(base, f);\n572:             each_node(index, f);\n573:         }\n574:         Kind::Slice { base, start, end, .. } => {\n575:             each_node(base, f);\n576:             if let Some(s) = start {\n577:                 each_node(s, f);\n578:             }\n579:             if let Some(e) = end {\n580:                 each_node(e, f);\n581:             }\n582:         }\n583:         Kind::Match { subject, arms, .. } => {\n584:             each_node(subject, f);\n585:             for arm in arms {\n586:                 if let Some(g) = &arm.guard {\n587:                     each_node(g, f);\n588:                 }\n589:                 each_node(&arm.body, f);\n590:             }\n591:         }\n592:     }\n593: }\n594: \n595: /// Whether `t` makes a self-call to `name` in a tail position: a call whose result is the\n596: /// function's result, with nothing left to do after it. This is what lets the js and py\n597: /// emitters lower a self-tail-recursive function to a loop, the constant-stack contract\n598: /// (kantord/toylang#141).\n599: ///\n600: /// Only a total `Match`'s arm bodies and a `Bind`'s body put their child in tail position; a\n601: /// partial `Match` wraps every arm body in `{some: ...}`, so nothing there is a tail call, and\n602: /// a call feeding an operator (`f(x) + 1`) is a genuine recursion the contract does not cover.\n603: pub fn has_tail_call(name: &str, t: &Tir) -> bool {\n604:     match &t.kind {\n605:         Kind::Call { func, .. } => func == name,\n606:         Kind::Bind { body, .. } => has_tail_call(name, body),\n607:         Kind::Match { arms, partial, .. } if !partial => {\n608:             arms.iter().any(|a| has_tail_call(name, &a.body))\n\n(Showing lines 519-608 of 612. Use offset=609 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\n/// Every node in the tree, `t` itself included, in no particular order. The backends each walk\n/// the tree their own way, gathering what their own target needs; this is for the questions\n/// that are the same on every target. Public so `offload::explain` can report on every\n/// sub-expression the same way. \npub fn each_node(t: &Tir, f: &mut impl FnMut(&Tir)) {\n    f(t);\n    match &t.kind {\n        Kind::Str(_)\n        | Kind::Int(_)\n        | Kind::Float(_)\n        | Kind::Var(_)\n        | Kind::Local(_)\n        | Kind::Input\n        | Kind::Inputs\n        | Kind::Lines\n        | Kind::Dsv { .. } => {}\n        Kind::VecLit(items) => items.iter().for_each(|i| each_node(i, f)),\n        Kind::RecordLit { fields } => fields.iter().for_each(|(_, v)| each_node(v, f)),\n        Kind::EnumLit { payload, .. } => {","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs","text":"\n/// Every node in the tree, `t` itself included, in no particular order. The backends each walk\n/// the tree their own way, gathering what their own target needs; this is for the questions\n/// that are the same on every target. Public so `offload::explain` can report on every\n/// sub-expression the same way. \npub fn each_node(t: &Tir, f: &mut impl FnMut(&Tir)) {\n    f(t);\n    match &t.kind {\n        Kind::Str(_)\n        | Kind::Int(_)\n        | Kind::Float(_)\n        | Kind::Var(_)\n        | Kind::Local(_)\n        | Kind::Input\n        | Kind::Inputs\n        | Kind::Lines\n        | Kind::Dsv { .. } => {}\n        Kind::VecLit(items) => items.iter().for_each(|i| each_node(i, f)),\n        Kind::RecordLit { fields } => fields.iter().for_each(|(_, v)| each_node(v, f)),\n        Kind::EnumLit { payload, .. } => {\n            if let Some(p) = payload {\n                each_node(p, f);\n            }\n        }\n        Kind::Call { arg, .. } => {\n            if let Some(a) = arg {\n                each_node(a, f);\n            }\n        }\n        Kind::Concat(l, r)\n        | Kind::Compare { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. }\n        | Kind::Logic { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. }\n        | Kind::Arith { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. } => {\n            each_node(l, f);\n            each_node(r, f);\n        }\n        Kind::Not(base) => each_node(base, f),\n        Kind::Bind { value, body, .. } => {\n            each_node(value, f);\n            each_node(body, f);\n        }\n        Kind::Map { source, body, .. } | Kind::OptMap { source, body, .. } => {\n            each_node(source, f);\n            each_node(body, f);\n        }\n        Kind::Select { source, pred, .. } => {\n            each_node(source, f);\n            each_node(pred, f);\n        }\n        Kind::Field { base, .. } | Kind::Unwrap { base } => each_node(base, f),\n        Kind::Builtin { arg, .. } => each_node(arg, f),\n        Kind::Index { base, index, .. } => {\n            each_node(base, f);\n            each_node(index, f);\n        }\n        Kind::Slice { base, start, end, .. } => {\n            each_node(base, f);\n            if let Some(s) = start {\n                each_node(s, f);\n            }\n            if let Some(e) = end {\n                each_node(e, f);\n            }\n        }\n        Kind::Match { subject, arms, .. } => {\n            each_node(subject, f);\n            for arm in arms {\n                if let Some(g) = &arm.guard {\n                    each_node(g, f);\n                }\n                each_node(&arm.body, f);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Whether `t` makes a self-call to `name` in a tail position: a call whose result is the\n/// function's result, with nothing left to do after it. This is what lets the js and py\n/// emitters lower a self-tail-recursive function to a loop, the constant-stack contract\n/// (kantord/toylang#141).\n///\n/// Only a total `Match`'s arm bodies and a `Bind`'s body put their child in tail position; a\n/// partial `Match` wraps every arm body in `{some: ...}`, so nothing there is a tail call, and\n/// a call feeding an operator (`f(x) + 1`) is a genuine recursion the contract does not cover.\npub fn has_tail_call(name: &str, t: &Tir) -> bool {\n    match &t.kind {\n        Kind::Call { func, .. } => func == name,\n        Kind::Bind { body, .. } => has_tail_call(name, body),\n        Kind::Match { arms, partial, .. } if !partial => {\n            arms.iter().any(|a| has_tail_call(name, &a.body))","lineStart":519,"lineEnd":608,"totalLines":612,"truncated":true}},"title":"src/tir.rs","time":{"start":1788464724266,"end":1788464724270}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Many exhaustive matches. Adding Kind variants means I need to update every exhaustive match. Let me check the ones that might have catch-all or be exhaustive:\n- tir.rs:357 flatten (catch-all unreachable — fine as long as SortBy isn't stream-typed; but the match must be exhaustive in Rust! A catch-all `_ => unreachable!` covers it. Yes there's `_ => unreachable!` at 423. So fine.\n\n- tir.rs:526 (each_node?), tir.rs:604 (has_tail_call?). Let me check those.\n- tags.rs walk and tag — need new arms.\n.\n- emit_rs.rs:795 (tail_stmts? — actually that's a different function), 1175 (expr — exhaustive match over Kind — need arms; but check if there's catch-all. Let me check each expr match for a wildcard. Most expr matches are exhaustive with no wildcard (e.g. Python expr at 423 — need arms for SortBy/MaxBy. \n\nLet me che