{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788464782754,"sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"todowrite","callID":"call_4210052ebef64f3ba0705757","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"todos":[{"content":"Add SortBy/MaxBy Kind variants to tir.rs (plus each_node arm)","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Add checker dispatch + sort_by_call/max_by_call in check/mod.rs, BUILTIN_NAMES","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update tags.rs walk/tag","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update check/linearity.rs stream_uses/any_node/calls_in","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Emit sort_by/max_by in py, jq, js, lua, go, rs, llvm backends + runtime C","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Add corpus cases for sort_by/max_by (incl empty, records, strings, refusals)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Add docs pages docs/reference/builtins/sort_by.md + max_by.md","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Update docs/examples/euler/26 to use max_by","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Run just check, fix failures; just fmt; clippy on touched code","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Commit per AGENTS.md with provenance line","status":"pending","priority":"high"}]},"output":"[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Add SortBy/MaxBy Kind variants to tir.rs (plus each_node arm)\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Add checker dispatch + sort_by_call/max_by_call in check/mod.rs, BUILTIN_NAMES\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Update tags.rs walk/tag\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Update check/linearity.rs stream_uses/any_node/calls_in\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Emit sort_by/max_by in py, jq, js, lua, go, rs, llvm backends + runtime C\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Add corpus cases for sort_by/max_by (incl empty, records, strings, refusals)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Add docs pages docs/reference/builtins/sort_by.md + max_by.md\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Update docs/examples/euler/26 to use max_by\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Run just check, fix failures; just fmt; clippy on touched code\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Commit per AGENTS.md with provenance line\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Add SortBy/MaxBy Kind variants to tir.rs (plus each_node arm)","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Add checker dispatch + sort_by_call/max_by_call in check/mod.rs, BUILTIN_NAMES","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update tags.rs walk/tag","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update check/linearity.rs stream_uses/any_node/calls_in","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Emit sort_by/max_by in py, jq, js, lua, go, rs, llvm backends + runtime C","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Add corpus cases for sort_by/max_by (incl empty, records, strings, refusals)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Add docs pages docs/reference/builtins/sort_by.md + max_by.md","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Update docs/examples/euler/26 to use max_by","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Run just check, fix failures; just fmt; clippy on touched code","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Commit per AGENTS.md with provenance line","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"10 todos","time":{"start":1788464782741,"end":1788464782750}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me look at how a backend test file works (backend_py.rs etc. and whether there's a test that runs corpus cases across all backends. The corpus.rs presumably runs all corpus YAML on all backends. And support::agreement_failures. So adding corpus YAML cases gives cross-backend coverage. Good.\n\nLet me also check how the docs harness gates slow fragments (TOYLANG_SLOW. Fine.\n\n.\n\nNow, let me think about the checker more: \n\nOne subtlety: `sort_by`/`max_by`'s source is a `Kind::Local(id)` that reads the piped subject. The subject's type is the full Vec<T>. Result type: `subject` (the Vec type). Good.\n\nBut wait — the pipe mechanism: `pipe()` synthesizes lhs, binds to a local, and checks rhs in a context with `ctx.subject = Some((value.ty.clone(), local))`. So in `v | sort_by(.key)`, when checking `sort_by(.key)`, `ctx.subject` = Some((Vec<T>, id)). My sort_by_call reads that. The `source` Tir: `Tir::new(subject, Kind::Local(id))`. Good — mirrors select_call/map_call.\n\n.\n\n\n\nNow — an important check: does the checker's `pipe` demand the right side use the subject? No — it just binds. And sort_by uses it via ctx.subject. Fine.\n\n\n\nNow — the checker's `call()` dispatch — sort_by needs `ctx.subject`. But what if sort_by is called without a pipe (like at program body, `sort_by(.x)` with no subject)? `ctx.subject` is None → error \"`sort_by` needs a subject, so it must follow `|`\". Good.\n\nBut wait — could sort_by be legitimately called with the Vec as a direct argument somehow? Like `sort_by([{a:2},{a:1}], .a)`? No unary calls. So no.\n\n\n\nHmm — but hold on. Let me reconsider: maybe the intended design is sort_by takes a *record* combining Vec+projection, since the language's \"something wanting two arguments takes a record\" (tir.rs comment: \"Each is unary,and so is every user function: something wanting two arguments takes a record, which is what a record literal is for in argument position\"). Hmm! That comment says two-argument things take a record. So maybe `sort_by({v: v, key: .key})`? But then `.key` — `.` would be unbound (no element. The projection needs `.` to be the element. So a record arg can't express the projection. Unless the projection is a named function reference? Like `sort_by({v: v, key: cycle_length})`? No first-class functions in this language. So the pipe form is the only way. The record convention is for two *value* arguments. Here the second \"argument\" is a projection expression that must see the element, so the pipe is required (exactly like map/select. I'm confident: `v | sort_by(.key)`. \n\n\n\nLet me also double check: does `map_call`'s subject require the pipe? Yes — \"`map` needs a subject, so it must follow `|`\". Same.\n\n.\n\n\n\nNow — implement. Let me start writing code. First tir.rs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_068cedd68001rhOJAZU6GTbu84","sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","messageID":"msg_068ceaed6001aGZyYkwFkVXdgo"}}
