{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788464796317,"sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_c1e76209e8b941d9885dd688","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs","oldString":"Select {\n        source: Box<Tir>,\n        param: LocalId,\n        pred: Box<Tir>,\n    },\n    /// Read `name` off `base`.","newString":"Select {\n        source: Box<Tir>,\n        param: LocalId,\n        pred: Box<Tir>,\n    },\n    /// `v | sort_by(.key)`, `v`'s entries in ascending order by the scalar the projection `body`\n    /// projects each entry to, ties keeping their original order (a stable sort, the way jq's\n    /// `sort_by` reads). Unlike `sort` no total order on `T` is needed: every backend orders\n    /// by the projected key, which the checker restricts to the same natively-ordered scalars\n    /// `sort` takes.\n    SortBy {\n        source: Box<Tir>,\n        param: LocalId,\n        body: Box<Tir>,\n    },\n    /// `v | max_by(.key)`, the entry whose projection `body` is greatest, `Opt<T>` because an\n    /// empty Vec has no maximum -- the same absence answer `max` gives (kantord/toylang#140).\n    /// Ties keep the first such entry, the way a stable maximum reads.\n\n    MaxBy {\n        source: Box<Tir>,\n        param: LocalId,\n        body: Box<Tir>,\n    },\n    /// Read `name` off `base`."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs\n@@ -121,8 +121,27 @@\n     source: Box<Tir>,\n     param: LocalId,\n     pred: Box<Tir>,\n },\n+/// `v | sort_by(.key)`, `v`'s entries in ascending order by the scalar the projection `body`\n+/// projects each entry to, ties keeping their original order (a stable sort, the way jq's\n+/// `sort_by` reads). Unlike `sort` no total order on `T` is needed: every backend orders\n+/// by the projected key, which the checker restricts to the same natively-ordered scalars\n+/// `sort` takes.\n+SortBy {\n+    source: Box<Tir>,\n+    param: LocalId,\n+    body: Box<Tir>,\n+},\n+/// `v | max_by(.key)`, the entry whose projection `body` is greatest, `Opt<T>` because an\n+/// empty Vec has no maximum -- the same absence answer `max` gives (kantord/toylang#140).\n+/// Ties keep the first such entry, the way a stable maximum reads.\n+\n+MaxBy {\n+    source: Box<Tir>,\n+    param: LocalId,\n+    body: Box<Tir>,\n+},\n /// Read `name` off `base`. How many Vec layers to descend through is `base.ty`'s doing and\n /// is not stored, so it cannot disagree with the type.\n Field {\n     base: Box<Tir>,\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/src/tir.rs\n@@ -121,8 +121,27 @@\n     source: Box<Tir>,\n     param: LocalId,\n     pred: Box<Tir>,\n },\n+/// `v | sort_by(.key)`, `v`'s entries in ascending order by the scalar the projection `body`\n+/// projects each entry to, ties keeping their original order (a stable sort, the way jq's\n+/// `sort_by` reads). Unlike `sort` no total order on `T` is needed: every backend orders\n+/// by the projected key, which the checker restricts to the same natively-ordered scalars\n+/// `sort` takes.\n+SortBy {\n+    source: Box<Tir>,\n+    param: LocalId,\n+    body: Box<Tir>,\n+},\n+/// `v | max_by(.key)`, the entry whose projection `body` is greatest, `Opt<T>` because an\n+/// empty Vec has no maximum -- the same absence answer `max` gives (kantord/toylang#140).\n+/// Ties keep the first such entry, the way a stable maximum reads.\n+\n+MaxBy {\n+    source: Box<Tir>,\n+    param: LocalId,\n+    body: Box<Tir>,\n+},\n /// Read `name` off `base`. How many Vec layers to descend through is `base.ty`'s doing and\n /// is not stored, so it cannot disagree with the type.\n Field {\n     base: Box<Tir>,\n","additions":19,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/tir.rs","time":{"start":1788464796313,"end":1788464796315}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_068cf12810017kQH0N2Ps9u1x8","sessionID":"ses_f97363172ffe9X2xJ1KPM1b5DB","messageID":"msg_068ceddb8001A7ZojEU5L5SqPl"}}
